      "problem": "Find $160\\%$ of $75,$ and then $150\\%$ of the result.",
      "worked_solution": "First, we find $160\\%$ of $75{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}160%\\times 75 & =\\frac{160}{100}\\times 75 \\\\  & =1.6\\times 75 \\\\  & =120\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we find $150\\%$ of the result $(120){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}150%\\times 120 & =\\frac{150}{100}\\times 120 \\\\  & =1.5\\times 120 \\\\  & =180\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the final answer is $180.$",
